@* Tag's Overview, written by hand after Alert's: colors and variants, links, icons
   and sizes, removable filters (previewed in each mode). Accessibility and See also come from the
   doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A tag is a small label for a keyword, a category or an applied filter; it can be a link, and the user can remove it. For a small status label or a count, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/badge">Badge</Anchor>. For choosing several values in a form, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/multi-select">MultiSelect</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Status and variants</Heading>
<TextBlock>A tag's status or accent sets its color, and its variant sets its weight. To set a tag's color, set <Code>Status</Code> or <Code>Accent</Code>. To set its weight, set <Code>Variant</Code>: <Code>Soft</Code> (the default), <Code>Solid</Code> or <Code>Outline</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-variants" />

<Heading Level="2">Links, icons, pills and sizes</Heading>
<TextBlock>A tag can be a link, show an icon and have rounded ends, in one of three sizes. To make a tag a link, set <Code>Href</Code>; to add an icon, set <Code>StartIcon</Code>. For rounded ends, as for topics or an announcement link above a heading, set <Code>Pill</Code>. To choose its size, set <Code>Size</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-links-sizes" />

<Heading Level="2">Removable</Heading>
<TextBlock>A removable tag has a remove control after its label. For a remove link that works on any page, such as to the current URL without that filter, set <Code>RemoveHref</Code>. To run C# on <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">interactive pages</Anchor>, set <Code>OnRemove</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="tag-remove" />
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>When a tag may render in either render mode, set both. Interactive pages use <Code>OnRemove</Code>, and static pages use the link.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With only <Code>OnRemove</Code>, static pages show no remove control at all.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>For a row of filters that a <Anchor Href="docs/components/filter-form">FilterForm</Anchor> applies, build each <Code>RemoveHref</Code> with <Code>Navigation.GetUriWithQueryParameter</Code>, so the rest of the URL stays.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The remove control has a name for screen readers. To set it for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>RemoveLabel</Code></td><td>The start of the remove control's name, followed by the tag's label, as in "Remove Blazor"</td><td>"Remove"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Tag Label="Blazor" Href="/topics/blazor" />

        @* An applied filter: a link on static pages, C# on interactive ones. *@
        <Tag Label="Status: Paid" Status="Status.Success"
             RemoveHref="@Navigation.GetUriWithQueryParameter("status", (string?)null)"
             OnRemove="ClearStatus" />
        """;
}
